{
  "$defs": {
    "BackboneType": {
      "description": "Feature-extractor family. ``RESNET`` and ``NONTRANSFORMER`` are the same CNN backbone\nunder two historical names; both were selectable from the config.",
      "enum": [
        "transformer",
        "resnet",
        "nontransformer"
      ],
      "title": "BackboneType",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "BlurKind": {
      "description": "Blur variants. Replaces the free-form ``blur_k`` strings, where a shipped config\nspelled the value ``\"guass\"`` and hit an unbound-local crash.",
      "enum": [
        "gauss",
        "median",
        "blur"
      ],
      "title": "BlurKind",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "OptimizerType": {
      "description": "``initialization.py`` hard-coded ``torch.optim.Adam`` while the config carried an unused\n``\"optimizer\": \"adam\"`` string; that string is now the field that actually selects one.",
      "enum": [
        "adam",
        "adamw",
        "sgd",
        "adadelta"
      ],
      "title": "OptimizerType",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "OutputType": {
      "description": "How a label image is written: ``2d`` (class id per pixel) or ``3d`` (RGB).\n\nThe config field used to be ``Literal[\"2d\", \"3d\"]`` while :mod:`sbb_pytorch.gt.render` kept a\nsecond spelling of its own; one definition now serves both, and ``render`` imports it from\nhere. The legacy CLI accepted any string for ``--type_output`` and then fell through both\n``if``/``elif`` branches, leaving ``img_poly`` unbound -- an ``UnboundLocalError`` rather than\na usage error, which is what ``parse`` replaces.",
      "enum": [
        "2d",
        "3d"
      ],
      "title": "OutputType",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "Page2Label": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "``custom_config_page2label.json`` -- which XML element names map to which class ids.\n\nThe legacy ``validate_configs`` required *exactly one* text region for the textline use\ncase; the shipped file defines three (``rest_as_paragraph``, ``header``, ``heading``,\n``marginalia``) so the rule contradicted the project's own config and is dropped. The\nduplicate value (both ``header`` and ``heading`` map to ``2``) is reported by\n:meth:`SBBConfig.warnings` rather than rejected, because it is present in the shipped file.\n\nThe five fields the legacy table carried and this model did not have -- ``case_label``,\n``artificial_class_label``, ``printspace_as_class_in_layout``, ``tableregion``,\n``noiseregion`` -- are here now, which is what lets a single-class config\n(``configs/textline.json``, ``n_classes: 3``) name what its own model predicts instead of\ninheriting the layout table's ids: its :attr:`case_label` is the line class and its\n:attr:`artificial_class_label` the boundary ring between lines. :meth:`all_regions` and\n:meth:`class_ids` keep naming only the elements they always named, so the inversion a\n``layout`` config produces is unchanged.",
      "properties": {
        "artificial_class_label": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Artificial Class Label"
        },
        "case_label": {
          "default": 1,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Case Label",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "columns_width": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "title": "Columns Width",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "graphicregions": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "title": "Graphicregions",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "imageregion": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Imageregion"
        },
        "noiseregion": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Noiseregion"
        },
        "printspace_as_class_in_layout": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Printspace As Class In Layout"
        },
        "separatorregion": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Separatorregion"
        },
        "tableregion": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Tableregion"
        },
        "textregions": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "title": "Textregions",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "use_case": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/UseCase"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "use_case"
      ],
      "title": "Page2Label",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ScalesConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "``scales_enhancement.json``. The legacy validator required ``0 < scale < 1``; kept.",
      "properties": {
        "scales": {
          "items": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "title": "Scales",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "scales"
      ],
      "title": "ScalesConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TaskType": {
      "description": "What the model predicts.\n\n``BINARIZATION`` and ``READING_ORDER`` were absent from the enum although both are shipped\nEynollah use cases, so a config naming either one failed to load.",
      "enum": [
        "segmentation",
        "classification",
        "enhancement",
        "binarization",
        "reading_order"
      ],
      "title": "TaskType",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "TransformerConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Vision-transformer geometry. Was seven flat ``transformer_*`` keys.",
      "properties": {
        "cnn_first": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Cnn First",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "layers": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Layers",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "mlp_head_units": {
          "items": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "title": "Mlp Head Units",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "num_heads": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Num Heads",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "num_patches_xy": {
          "maxItems": 2,
          "minItems": 2,
          "prefixItems": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "integer"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Num Patches Xy",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "patchsize_x": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "title": "Patchsize X",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "patchsize_y": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "title": "Patchsize Y",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "projection_dim": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "title": "Projection Dim",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "num_patches_xy",
        "patchsize_x",
        "patchsize_y",
        "projection_dim",
        "mlp_head_units",
        "layers",
        "num_heads"
      ],
      "title": "TransformerConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "UseCase": {
      "description": "What is being labelled -- the one spelling :class:`Page2Label` and\n:class:`~sbb_pytorch.gt.GroundTruthConfig` share.\n\n``gt/generator.py`` used to carry its own seven-member copy while this module shipped five\n(no ``binarization``, no ``reading_order``), so a value one accepted the other rejected. The\ngenerator's set wins: both are real use cases -- ``binarization``'s single class is the print\nspace, and ``reading_order``'s labels come from ``.case`` files -- and the legacy code\ncompared ``config_params['use_case']`` against four string literals with ``or``, then required\n``use_case == 'layout'``; any other value fell through both branches and wrote nothing,\nsilently.",
      "enum": [
        "layout",
        "textline",
        "word",
        "glyph",
        "printspace",
        "binarization",
        "reading_order"
      ],
      "title": "UseCase",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "The whole configuration for one run: model, training, augmentation and directories.\n\nEvery field carries a default, so a config may name only what it cares about -- the old\nbracket-indexing made an omitted optional key a ``KeyError``.",
